  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Capacity Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to build capacity and develop a network of African conservationists who can implement grassroots conservation actions for the West African manatee (Trichechus senegalensis), collect and analyze samples that are critically needed to increase understanding of the species, and to disseminate results. The project will: 1) Develop capacity and resources of protected area managers and field personnel to take action against key threats to manatees in Central Africa. Activities include training at workshops, providing guidance, giving field sampling equipment, providing standardized datasheets and materials for data collection, maintaining an internet discussion group for African manatee conservationists, and working with collaborators to report and disseminate results. 2) Increase sampling for first regional population level assessment of West African manatee genetic diversity, feeding ecology and longevity. Activities include increasing surveys to determine manatee presence and habitat use, collecting biological samples, determining distinct populations, analyzing manatee diet, using ear bones of manatee carcasses to determine species longevity, and collecting other samples to determine baseline health paramaters for manatees.</narrative>
  </description>
